---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Methodology — groundwaterwatch" page="methodology">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Two data products. Public domain. Aggregated to NUTS-2 regions. We
    document everything here because awareness work without methodology
    isn't journalism, it's vibes.
  </p>

  <h2>Current week (this week's map)</h2>
  <p>
    The current map is mirrored directly from
    <a href="https://nasagrace.unl.edu/">nasagrace.unl.edu</a>, which is
    NASA Goddard's operational percentile visualization run in partnership
    with the National Drought Mitigation Center. Latency: 2–9 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is NASA's official operational product. We do not modify it, we
    only mirror it for stable hosting.
  </p>

  <h2>Multi-year trend (the chart)</h2>
  <p>
    The trend chart is our independent zonal aggregation of the
    <a href="https://disc.gsfc.nasa.gov/datasets/GRACEDADM_CLSM025GL_7D_3.0/summary">
      GRACEDADM_CLSM025GL_7D V3.0
    </a> final-archive product from NASA GES DISC. Weekly cadence, 0.25°
    (~25 km) resolution, NetCDF format, NASA public domain. Coverage
    February 2003 → present, with a 3–6 month archive latency.
  </p>
  <p>
    The percentile is pre-computed by NASA against the 1948–2014 baseline.
    We aggregate the per-cell values to NUTS-2 polygons (Eurostat 2021
    boundaries, 1:1M scale) using cosine-of-latitude area weighting, then
    compute the share of polygon area that falls into each U.S. Drought
    Monitor severity band (D4 ≤ 2nd percentile, D3 ≤ 5th, D2 ≤ 10th,
    D1 ≤ 20th, D0 ≤ 30th).
  </p>

  <h2>Resolution floor</h2>
  <p>
    The native 0.25° grid corresponds to ~25 km cells. Romania has ~380
    cells; Hungary ~150. <strong>NUTS-2</strong> is the smallest geography
    we report. NUTS-3 (counties / județe / megyék) is too coarse for a 25 km
    grid to characterize defensibly. Some NUTS-2 regions are themselves
    very small: Budapest (HU11) gets only one valid cell, București-Ilfov
    (RO32) gets three. Those numbers are flagged with a low-confidence
    indicator in the per-country tables.
  </p>

  <h2>What this dashboard does <em>not</em> measure</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Individual wells. The product is a modeled aquifer-storage anomaly,
      not a well registry.
    </li>
    <li>Drinking-water quality, salinity, or contamination.</li>
    <li>Surface water — rivers, lakes, reservoirs. Those are separate products.</li>
    <li>
      Sub-NUTS-2 detail. Do not interpret a single 25 km cell as
      authoritative for any specific village or city block within it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Real-time conditions. The mission cadence is weekly at best.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Source code & licenses</h2>
  <p>
    Pipeline and frontend are MIT-licensed at
    <a href="https://github.com/sunlesshalo/groundwaterwatch">github.com/sunlesshalo/groundwaterwatch</a>.
    NASA data is public domain. Eurostat boundaries are CC-BY 4.0.
  </p>
</Base>
